CowSwapModule_CancelOrder
├── when order is unknown
│   ├── it should revert with CowSwapModule_UnknownOrder (zero id)
│   └── it should revert with CowSwapModule_UnknownOrder (arbitrary id)
├── when caller is not the module owner
│   ├── it should revert with OwnableUnauthorizedAccount (attacker)
│   └── it should revert with OwnableUnauthorizedAccount (paymentRails)
├── given order is already cancelled
│   └── it should revert with CowSwapModule_OrderAlreadyCancelled
├── given order is already filled by solver
│   ├── it should revert with CowSwapModule_OrderAlreadyFilled (exact fill)
│   ├── it should revert with CowSwapModule_OrderAlreadyFilled (overfilled)
│   └── given order is partially filled it should succeed
├── given order is pending
│   ├── given solver already pulled sell token
│   │   ├── it should set cancelled to true
│   │   ├── it should emit OrderCancelled with zero return amount
│   │   ├── it should not transfer any tokens
│   │   └── it should not revert
│   └── given sell token is still in module
│       ├── it should set cancelled to true
│       ├── it should leave max approval unchanged
│       ├── it should transfer sell tokens back to paymentRails
│       ├── it should emit OrderCancelled event
│       └── it should cause isValidSignature to return FAILURE
└── full lifecycle
    └── it should execute then cancel then recover tokens
